WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.855 --> 00:00:15.996
down, please, Mr.

2
00:00:16.036 --> 00:00:17.196
Fleming. Come with me."

3
00:00:17.956 --> 00:00:18.996
Mr. Beck stood up.

4
00:00:19.016 --> 00:00:21.237
"You kids should run along."

5
00:00:22.197 --> 00:00:24.318
The secretary led the older man away.

6
00:00:25.058 --> 00:00:26.838
Henry and Maggie wandered outside.

7
00:00:26.858 --> 00:00:29.999
"That was weird," Maggie said.

8
00:00:30.019 --> 00:00:32.540
"Mr. Fleming seemed really mad.

9
00:00:33.640 --> 00:00:36.522
Maybe he's the one who made the threatening comment on the website!"

10
00:00:37.682 --> 00:00:39.783
"That's exactly what I was thinking."

11
00:00:40.184 --> 00:00:40.964
Henry frowned.

12
00:00:40.984 --> 00:00:43.906
"But why would he steal Mrs.

13
00:00:43.986 --> 00:00:45.046
Sweet's candy?

14
00:00:45.967 --> 00:00:50.049
And if he left that comment, why would he delete it if he's still mad?"

15
00:00:50.069 --> 00:00:54.591
"I don't know," Maggie said.

16
00:00:54.611 --> 00:00:56.953
"We should tell Jackson about this, though.

17
00:00:57.873 --> 00:00:59.154
Maybe he can figure it out."

18
00:00:59.934 --> 00:01:01.175
She looked at the town clock.

19
00:01:01.195 --> 00:01:02.916
"It's getting late.

20
00:01:03.276 --> 00:01:04.577
We need to finish our float."

21
00:01:05.597 --> 00:01:07.498
"Okay, let's go," Henry said.

22
00:01:07.518 --> 00:01:09.919
"We'll tell Jackson about Mr.

23
00:01:09.979 --> 00:01:11.480
Fleming the next time we see him."

24
00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:14.281
They walked back to the lemonade stand.

25
00:01:16.882 --> 00:01:18.182
Nathan was there with Cole.

26
00:01:19.143 --> 00:01:23.004
Henry and Maggie quickly told them what they'd found out during their trip into town.

27
00:01:23.024 --> 00:01:24.565
"I know Mr.

28
00:01:24.605 --> 00:01:26.446
Fleming," Cole said when they finished.

29
00:01:27.106 --> 00:01:28.047
"He lives on my block."

30
00:01:28.067 --> 00:01:30.307
"Is he always that cranky?"

31
00:01:30.608 --> 00:01:31.348
Maggie asked.

32
00:01:32.404 --> 00:01:33.165
Cole shrugged.

33
00:01:33.185 --> 00:01:35.366
"Yeah, he's pretty cranky.

34
00:01:36.286 --> 00:01:38.388
But my mom says he's like a yappy dog.

35
00:01:38.948 --> 00:01:40.389
His bark is worse than his bite."

36
00:01:43.451 --> 00:01:46.773
"Do you think he could have left that nasty website comment?"

37
00:01:47.033 --> 00:01:47.793
Henry asked.

38
00:01:48.834 --> 00:01:49.795
"Or stolen Mrs.

39
00:01:49.855 --> 00:01:50.655
Sweet's candy?"

40
00:01:51.596 --> 00:01:54.377
"I doubt he'd steal anything," Cole said.

41
00:01:54.397 --> 00:01:56.218
"I don't know about the comment."

42
00:01:57.279 --> 00:01:58.380
Maggie looked restless.

43
00:01:59.348 --> 00:02:03.231
"If you guys want to keep talking about this, let's do it while we work on our float,"

44
00:02:03.592 --> 00:02:04.092
she said.

45
00:02:04.112 --> 00:02:07.135
"Nathan, can you watch the lemonade stand?"

46
00:02:08.055 --> 00:02:11.598
Nathan agreed, and The Lemonade Detectives headed into Maggie's house.

47
00:02:12.619 --> 00:02:16.142
Her father was in the backyard putting gasoline into the lawn tractor.

48
00:02:16.162 --> 00:02:18.904
"Are you ready for tomorrow, Dad?"

49
00:02:19.104 --> 00:02:19.885
Maggie asked.

50
00:02:19.905 --> 00:02:23.028
"Almost." Her father scratched his head.

51
00:02:23.048 --> 00:02:24.969
"There's just one problem.

52
00:02:26.010 --> 00:02:28.112
I've looked everywhere, but I can't find the hitch pin."

53
00:02:29.288 --> 00:02:30.409
"What's a hitch pin?"

54
00:02:30.629 --> 00:02:31.450
Cole asked.

55
00:02:31.470 --> 00:02:36.493
"It's the part that attaches our float to the tractor," Henry explained.

56
00:02:36.513 --> 00:02:40.436
"We'll definitely need it for the parade tomorrow.

57
00:02:41.516 --> 00:02:44.739
Maybe I should go over to Newman's Auto Shop and get another one."

58
00:02:45.679 --> 00:02:46.580
"Good idea, Henry."

59
00:02:47.220 --> 00:02:49.562
Maggie's dad pulled some bills out of his pocket.

60
00:02:49.582 --> 00:02:52.384
"This should be enough money to buy a new one."

61
00:02:56.446 --> 00:02:58.448
Soon Henry was biking to the auto shop.

62
00:02:59.448 --> 00:03:02.690
When he arrived, a fancy black convertible was parked out front.

63
00:03:03.851 --> 00:03:05.351
Its hood was up, and Mr.

64
00:03:05.411 --> 00:03:06.812
Newman was looking at the engine.

65
00:03:06.832 --> 00:03:08.393
"Hi, Mr.

66
00:03:08.433 --> 00:03:09.614
Newman," Henry said.

67
00:03:09.634 --> 00:03:11.895
"Isn't that the mayor's car?"

68
00:03:12.835 --> 00:03:13.836
Mr. Newman nodded.

69
00:03:13.856 --> 00:03:18.138
"He dropped it off for a tune-up so it will be ready for tomorrow's parade."

70
00:03:19.179 --> 00:03:20.079
Henry told Mr.

71
00:03:20.120 --> 00:03:21.040
Newman what he needed.

72
00:03:22.161 --> 00:03:23.641
Mr. Newman pointed inside.

73
00:03:23.661 --> 00:03:26.603
"My daughter is in the office," he said.

74
00:03:26.623 --> 00:03:28.004
"She'll help you."

75
00:03:28.888 --> 00:03:30.609
"Thanks." Henry went inside.

76
00:03:33.031 --> 00:03:35.292
He immediately recognized the girl in the office.

77
00:03:35.312 --> 00:03:38.434
"Oh, hi, Jade," he said.

78
00:03:38.454 --> 00:03:40.396
"I forgot that Mr.

79
00:03:40.456 --> 00:03:41.456
Newman is your dad."

80
00:03:41.476 --> 00:03:44.799
"Yeah, lucky me," Jade muttered.

81
00:03:45.399 --> 00:03:46.500
She sounded grouchy.

82
00:03:46.520 --> 00:03:48.241
"What do you want?"

83
00:03:49.302 --> 00:03:50.042
Henry told her.

84
00:03:50.763 --> 00:03:53.524
Jade grabbed a hitch pin out of a bin behind the counter.

85
00:03:53.544 --> 00:03:56.627
"Thanks," Henry said, handing her the money.

86
00:03:56.647 --> 00:04:02.138
"By the way, Snake told me your band had to drop out of the parade.

87
00:04:02.958 --> 00:04:03.879
Sorry about that."

88
00:04:03.899 --> 00:04:06.800
"I'm not sorry," Jade snapped.

89
00:04:07.701 --> 00:04:10.362
"Snake's the one who wanted to sign up for the parade.

90
00:04:11.503 --> 00:04:14.524
He thought being on TV would help our band get famous."

91
00:04:15.805 --> 00:04:16.625
Just then Mr.

92
00:04:16.646 --> 00:04:17.286
Newman entered.

93
00:04:17.306 --> 00:04:19.327
"What's taking so long?"

94
00:04:19.547 --> 00:04:20.768
he asked Jade with a frown.

95
00:04:20.788 --> 00:04:24.109
"You're supposed to be helping me with the mayor's car.

96
00:04:25.050 --> 00:04:28.552
I need to drop it off at the high school parking lot by the end of the day."

97
00:04:29.568 --> 00:04:31.169
"The high school parking lot?"

98
00:04:31.349 --> 00:04:32.069
Henry said.

99
00:04:32.089 --> 00:04:34.410
"Why are you taking it there?"

100
00:04:35.350 --> 00:04:36.391
Mr. Newman shrugged.

101
00:04:36.411 --> 00:04:38.392
"That's where the parade starts.

102
00:04:39.372 --> 00:04:44.574
I suppose the mayor wants it waiting there for him when everyone gathers for the parade tomorrow afternoon."

103
00:04:44.594 --> 00:04:47.235
"I'll be out to help you in a minute.

104
00:04:48.256 --> 00:04:52.117
I'm waiting on a customer," Jade told her father, waving toward Henry.

105
00:04:52.138 --> 00:04:57.020
"Well, stop gossiping about your silly band and finish up," Mr.

106
00:04:57.080 --> 00:04:57.740
Newman said.

107
00:04:58.452 --> 00:05:02.995
"Maybe you'll be a rock star someday, but for right now you have a job to do."

108
00:05:03.015 --> 00:05:05.737
"Whatever," Jade muttered.

109
00:05:05.757 --> 00:05:07.718
"Here's your change, Henry."

110
00:05:08.739 --> 00:05:12.501
She shoved some coins at Henry and then stomped out of the office with a scowl.

111
00:05:15.764 --> 00:05:18.045
Soon Henry was back on his bike, heading for home.

112
00:05:19.086 --> 00:05:22.148
As he passed the newspaper office, he saw Jackson near the entrance.

113
00:05:22.168 --> 00:05:23.829
"Hi there!"

114
00:05:24.029 --> 00:05:25.570
Henry called, stopping his bike.

115
00:05:26.651 --> 00:05:28.072
"I'm glad I ran into you.

116
00:05:28.972 --> 00:05:31.374
Something weird happened a little while ago."

117
00:05:32.375 --> 00:05:33.716
He told Jackson about Mr.

118
00:05:33.776 --> 00:05:35.477
Fleming's visit to the mayor's office.

119
00:05:36.458 --> 00:05:37.298
Jackson nodded.

120
00:05:37.318 --> 00:05:40.060
"Yes, I already heard about that," he said.

121
00:05:40.080 --> 00:05:44.784
"I also just heard that the mayor is seriously thinking about canceling the parade!"
